# ============================================================
# Track Maker Exercise Pack           format: tmex-v1
# ============================================================
# Plain-text, human-editable exercise definitions for the
# Practice Tools > Scales and Arpeggios tools. One file may
# hold any number of [exercise] blocks; the app will read
# every block in every .tmex file it's pointed at (loader is
# not implemented yet — this is the file format only).
#
# ---- HOW TO ADD AN EXERCISE ----------------------------------
#   1. Copy an existing [exercise] block, including its blank
#      line at the end, and paste it after the last one.
#   2. Fill in the fields below (see FIELDS).
#   3. Write the tab. Each note occupies a fixed 4-character
#      slot: two dashes, then the fret number right-aligned in
#      the last two characters, dash-padded.
#        fret 0   -> "---0"
#        fret 3   -> "---3"
#        fret 12  -> "--12"
#        no note  -> "----"
#      Every column must have a fret on exactly one string and
#      dashes on the other five — one note per step (single
#      note line, not chord strums).
#   4. String order is fixed, top to bottom: e B G D A E
#      (high e first, low E last — standard tab convention).
#   5. Long exercises wrap: split the tab into chunks of six
#      lines (same string order each time), separated by a
#      single blank line, like sheet music wrapping to the next
#      row. All six lines within one chunk must be the same
#      length; chunks don't need to match each other's length
#      (the last one is often shorter). The app reads every
#      chunk in order and joins each string's lines end-to-end
#      to rebuild the full sequence — so chunk 2 continues
#      exactly where chunk 1 left off, with no notes skipped or
#      repeated at the seam. The tab ends at the next
#      [exercise] line or end of file.
#
# ---- FIELDS ----------------------------------------------------
#   id        unique slug (lowercase, digits, hyphens only)
#   name      display name shown in the app
#   type      "scale" or "chord"  (chord = arpeggio exercise)
#   root      C C# D D# E F F# G G# A A# B
#   scale     scale-type key — scales only. Must match a key in
#             the app's SCALE_TYPES table, e.g. major, minor,
#             harmonicMinor, melodicMinor, majPent, minPent,
#             blues, dorian, phrygian, lydian, mixolydian, locrian
#   quality   chord-quality key — chords only. Must match a key
#             in the app's chordIntervals table, e.g. major,
#             minor, dim, aug, sus2, sus4, 6, m6, dom7, maj7,
#             min7, m7b5, dim7, 7sus4, add9, dom9, maj9, min9
#   position  practice position number (1 = includes open
#             strings; the app currently supports positions
#             1 through 11, each a 5-fret window)
#   frets     inclusive fret range covered, for reference only
#             (not re-derived from the tab — informational)
#   formula   scale/chord degree formula, hyphen-separated, for
#             reference/display only
#
# Lines starting with # anywhere in the file are comments and
# are ignored by the parser. Blank lines outside the tab section
# (between fields, or between exercises) are also ignored.
# ============================================================

